     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If datasetInput2 is not the problem, you might also try googleCharts; it is less complete but potentially more reliable when used with Shiny.<div><a href=\"https://github.com/jcheng5/googleCharts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jcheng5/googleCharts&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792404090940000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vSMvkuoIodpraOSDM2Aof\">https://github.com/jcheng5/googleCharts</a><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>Ideally this approach would be folded into googleVis but neither the googleVis maintainers nor I have had the time to do that.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
